# Chaos: the helper's settings survive death, relog, crashes and restarts (mods/game_helper/helper.lua; after 0001-0066).
# Owner: the helper's settings reset when the character died. The helper unblocked saves at the end of every UI reload
# (onLoadHelperData), loaded or not, and a helper.json it could not read (missing, cut short by a client closed on the
# death screen, not JSON) gave defaults that the next save wrote over the file. Now ChaosHelperSave (overlay
# game_helperrotation/helpersave.lua, tested with a death and relogin) decides: saves only after this character's file
# was read; a checked write through .tmp with a .bak of the last good file; a broken file is read from .bak / .tmp or
# kept as .broken; saveSettings is debounced (500 ms) and death (g_game.onDeath), logout and unload write at once.
# Without the overlay module the old code runs.
